.TH CRABTURE 1 "" "crabture @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
crabture \- screenshot capture, annotation and image management
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crabture
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIIMAGE\fR...]
.br
.B crabture
.B \-\-capture
.I MODE
[\fB\-\-delay\fR \fISECONDS\fR] [\fB\-\-folder\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-\-after\fR \fIeditor\fR|\fIsave\fR]
[\fB\-\-clipboard\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-hide\fR]
.br
.B crabture
.B \-\-directory
.I DIR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Crabture
is a lightweight screenshot tool and image annotator for Linux. It can
capture the screen, annotate images with arrows, shapes, text, numbered
steps, blur and pixelation, apply image effects, and browse and bulk-rename
the images in a folder.
.PP
If one
.I IMAGE
is given, it is opened in the editor on start-up and the gallery shows the
folder it lives in (unless
.B \-\-directory
is also given). If several images are given they open as one session: the
first is edited and the gallery lists just those files.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.I IMAGE...
Image file(s) to open on launch.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-directory " " \fIDIR\fR
Populate the gallery with the images in
.I DIR
(default: \fI~/Downloads/Crabshots\fR).
.TP
.BI \-\-capture " MODE"
Take a screenshot. If Crabture is already running the request is handed to that
instance. By default the shot opens in the editor (see
.BR \-\-after ).
.I MODE
is one of
.BR region ,
.BR fullscreen ,
.BR window ,
.B monitor
or
.BR scroll .
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " SECONDS"
Wait
.I SECONDS
before capturing.
.TP
.BI \-\-folder " DIR"
Save the screenshot in
.I DIR
instead of the capture folder chosen in Configure.
.TP
.BI \-\-after " editor" | save
.B editor
opens the screenshot in Crabture,
.B save
only saves it and shows a desktop notification (no window is opened).
Default: as chosen in Configure.
.TP
.B \-\-clipboard
Also copy the screenshot to the clipboard.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-hide
Do not hide the Crabture window while capturing.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-integration
Add the "Edit with Crabture" and "Open Directory with Crabture" entries to
Nautilus (right\-click, Scripts). The package does this automatically the first
time Crabture starts.
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-integration
Remove the entries added by
.BR \-\-install\-integration .
.TP
.B \-\-install\-integration
Add the "Edit with Crabture" and "Open Directory with Crabture" entries to
Nautilus (right\-click, Scripts). The package does this automatically the first
time Crabture starts.
.TP
.B \-\-remove\-integration
Remove the entries added by
.BR \-\-install\-integration .
.TP
.B \-\-register\-hotkeys
Give the capture shortcuts saved in Configure \(en Capture to the desktop
(GNOME custom keyboard shortcuts via
.BR gsettings (1),
or Xfce via
.BR xfconf\-query (1)).
Existing shortcuts are not overwritten; keys already in use are skipped.
.TP
.B \-\-unregister\-hotkeys
Remove the shortcuts added by
.BR \-\-register\-hotkeys .
.TP
.B \-\-backend\-info
Print which screen-capture backend Crabture would use on this system and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a help message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Downloads/Crabshots
Default folder for captures and for the gallery (changeable in Configure \(en Capture).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Crabture detects the session type (X11 or Wayland). On Wayland, screenshots
are taken through the xdg-desktop-portal Screenshot interface; on X11 the Qt
grab or an installed helper such as
.BR maim (1)
is used.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tesseract (1),
.BR gsettings (1),
.BR xdotool (1)
